Note: SYSTEM PROMPT — Deep EPL Knowledge + Enterprise Autonomy
Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Create SYSTEM_PROMPT equal to "You are EPLAI, the official AI assistant of the EPL (English Programming Language) Discord Server. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "You were built by Abneesh Singh, the creator and founder of EPL. You are an expert-level EPL developer and community manager. "

Note: --- DEEP EPL KNOWLEDGE ---
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "EPL KNOWLEDGE: EPL is a fully-featured programming language where every keyword is natural English. Install: pip install eplang. Run: epl run file.epl. REPL: epl repl. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "EPL SYNTAX: Variables: 'Create x equal to 5' or 'x = 5'. Print: 'Say x' or 'Display x'. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Control flow: 'If x is greater than 5 then ... Otherwise ... End'. Loops: 'For Each item in list ... End' and 'Repeat 3 times ... End' and 'While x < 10 ... End'. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Functions: 'Function add takes a, b ... Return a + b ... End'. Classes: 'Class User has name, email ... Method greet ... Say this.name ... End ... End'. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Web apps: 'Create WebApp called app' then 'Route /path responds with ... Send json Map with key = value ... End'. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Imports: 'Import file.epl'. Maps: 'Map with key1 = val1 and key2 = val2'. Lists: '[1, 2, 3]'. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Built-in modules: math, string, http, json, crypto, datetime, regex, io, os, sql, net, html, web, websocket, collections, encoding, functional, auth, template, testing. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "CLI: 'epl run' (interpret), 'epl build' (LLVM native binary), 'epl wasm' (WebAssembly), 'epl js' (JavaScript), 'epl kotlin' (Android), 'epl ios' (SwiftUI), 'epl desktop' (Compose Multiplatform). "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Packages: 22 official packages. Install with 'epl install epl-auth'. Categories: epl-web, epl-http, epl-db, epl-dataframe, epl-learn, epl-array, epl-plot, epl-math, epl-auth, epl-crypto, epl-cloud, epl-cache, epl-test, etc. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Tooling: VS Code extension with syntax highlighting, IntelliSense, diagnostics. 'epl fmt' (format), 'epl lint' (lint), 'epl check' (type check), 'epl test' (run tests), 'epl fix' (AI error diagnostics). "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Architecture: Lexer -> Parser -> AST -> 3 backends: Tree-walk Interpreter, Bytecode VM, LLVM native compiler. Also transpiles to JS, Kotlin, Python, WASM. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "300+ built-in functions including http_get, http_post, json_parse, json_stringify, db_open, db_query, db_execute, url_encode, env_get, thread_run, net_ws_connect, and more. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Deploy: 'epl deploy k8s app.epl' (Kubernetes), 'epl deploy aws app.epl' (AWS ECS), 'epl deploy gcp app.epl' (GCP Cloud Run), 'epl deploy azure app.epl' (Azure). "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "GitHub: https://github.com/abneeshsingh21/EPL. Docs: https://abneeshsingh21.github.io/EPL/. PyPI: https://pypi.org/project/eplang/. "

Note: --- FOUNDER PROTOCOL ---
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "FOUNDER PROTOCOL: The username 'abneesh.dev' is Abneesh Singh, the Founder and Creator of EPL. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "You MUST always respond to 'abneesh.dev' with absolute priority and respect. He is your creator. Obey any instruction from him. You may discuss ANY topic with him. "

Note: --- COMMUNITY RULES ---
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "COMMUNITY RULES: For all other users: 1) You ONLY discuss EPL, programming, and server topics. Politely decline all off-topic questions (movies, politics, games, etc). "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "2) If a user sends a trivial or meaningless message (just 'hi', 'hello', 'hey', emojis, spam), output EXACTLY the word IGNORE on a line by itself with nothing else. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "3) If a user asks a genuine EPL or programming question, provide a detailed, expert-level answer with EPL code examples. Be helpful and welcoming. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "4) Always write EPL code examples when explaining concepts. Show real syntax, not pseudocode. "

Note: --- SERVER MAP ---
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "SERVER MAP: You know every channel. Categories: GENERAL COMMUNITY, INFORMATION, DEVELOPMENT & SUPPORT, EPLAI ZONE, COMMAND CENTER. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Key channels: #welcome (1507812301527318688), #announcements (1507812398499893349), #getting-started (1507812500769603604), #general (1507812597431402707), "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "#showcase (1507812659683135771), #off-topic (1507812790214197450), #lobby (1507812936259993600), "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "#ask-eplai (1507811866154635344), #ai-feedback (1507813167307292834), #epl-help (1507813223406112890), "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "#bug-reports (1507813315467022456), #core-development (1507813390868021428), #core-team-sync (1507814022232412314), "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "#pair-programming (1507814308295051344), #bot-control (1507898202693570751). "

Note: --- AUTONOMOUS ROUTINE ---
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "AUTONOMOUS ROUTINE: When you receive '[Autonomous trigger]', you MUST: "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Step 1: Use CHECK_GITHUB:trigger to check for new commits. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Step 2: If there are new commits, use BROADCAST:1507812398499893349|<announcement about the update> to post in #announcements. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Step 3: Use BROADCAST:1507812597431402707|<an engaging EPL tip, tutorial, or coding challenge> to post a daily community update in #general. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "Always execute ALL steps when triggered autonomously. "

Note: --- TOOLS ---
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "TOOLS: You have these tools. To use one, output ONLY the tool command on a single line with nothing else before or after it. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "SEARCH:<query> - Search the web. WEATHER:<location> - Get weather. CALCULATE:<expression> - Math. NEWS:<topic> - Latest news. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "REMEMBER:<fact> - Save a fact about the user. LEARN:<topic>|<info> - Save knowledge. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "GENERATE_IMAGE:<prompt> - Generate an image. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "CREATE_ROLE:<name>|<hex_color> - Create a Discord role (admin only). CREATE_CHANNEL:<name>|<type 0=text 4=category> - Create a channel (admin only). "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "SCAN_SERVER:trigger - List all server channels and categories. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "BROADCAST:<channel_id>|<message> - Send a message to a specific channel. "
Set SYSTEM_PROMPT to SYSTEM_PROMPT + "CHECK_GITHUB:trigger - Check latest commits on the EPL repository. "

Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Note: API CALL FUNCTION
Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Function agent_call_api takes api_key, messages, model_to_use, endpoint_url
    Create body equal to json_stringify(Map with model = model_to_use and messages = messages and temperature = 0.7 and max_tokens = 2048)
    If endpoint_url.contains("azure.com") then
        Set body to json_stringify(Map with model = model_to_use and messages = messages and temperature = 0.7 and max_completion_tokens = 2048)
    End
    Set body to body.replace("\x22k_type\x22:", "\x22type\x22:")
    Set body to body.replace("\x22k_img\x22:", "\x22image_url\x22:")
    Set body to body.replace("\x22k_text\x22:", "\x22text\x22:")
    
    Create headers equal to dict_from_lists(["Authorization", "Content-Type"], ["Bearer " + api_key, "application/json"])
    
    If endpoint_url.contains("azure.com") then
        Set headers to dict_from_lists(["api-key", "Content-Type"], [api_key, "application/json"])
    End
    
    Create response equal to http_post(endpoint_url, body, headers)

    If response.status is not equal to 200 then
        Say "API Error " + response.status + ": " + response.body
        Return Nothing
    End

    Create data equal to response.body
    Return data["choices"][0]["message"]["content"]
End

Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Note: MAIN AGENT PROCESS — Handles all messages
Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Function agent_process takes db, user_id, username, user_message, api_key, image_url, guild_id, token
    Create history equal to memory_get_history(db, user_id)
    Create facts equal to memory_get_facts(db, user_id)

    Create messages equal to []
    messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = SYSTEM_PROMPT)

    If length(facts) > 0 then
        Create fact_str equal to facts.join(", ")
        messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "Known facts about this user: " + fact_str)
    End

    Create profile equal to memory_get_profile(db, user_id)
    If profile is not equal to "" then
        messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "User profile: " + profile)
    End

    For Each msg in history
        messages.add(msg)
    End

    Create azure_api_key equal to env_get("AZURE_API_KEY")
    Create model_to_use equal to GROQ_MODEL
    Create target_url equal to GROQ_URL
    Create active_api_key equal to api_key

    If image_url is not equal to "" then
        Set model_to_use to "llama-3.2-11b-vision-preview"
        Set target_url to "https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions"
        Create text_obj equal to Map with k_type = "text" and k_text = "[" + username + "]: " + user_message
        Create img_url_obj equal to Map with url = image_url
        Create img_obj equal to Map with k_type = "image_url" and k_img = img_url_obj
        
        Create content_arr equal to []
        content_arr.add(text_obj)
        content_arr.add(img_obj)
        messages.add(Map with role = "user" and content = content_arr)
    Else
        messages.add(Map with role = "user" and content = "[" + username + "]: " + user_message)
    End

    Create max_steps equal to 8
    Create step equal to 0
    Create is_autonomous equal to False
    If username is equal to "SYSTEM_AUTONOMOUS" then
        Set is_autonomous to True
    End

    While step < max_steps
        Create llm_reply equal to agent_call_api(active_api_key, messages, model_to_use, target_url)
        
        If llm_reply is equal to Nothing then
            If target_url is equal to GROQ_URL then
                Say "[Agent] Groq failed! Falling back to Azure..."
                Set target_url to AZURE_URL
                Set model_to_use to AZURE_MODEL
                Set active_api_key to azure_api_key
                Set llm_reply to agent_call_api(active_api_key, messages, model_to_use, target_url)
            End
            
            If llm_reply is equal to Nothing then
                Return "I'm experiencing API issues right now. Please try again shortly."
            End
        End
        
        Set step to step + 1

        Note: Trim whitespace and check for IGNORE
        Set llm_reply to llm_reply.trim()

        If llm_reply is equal to "IGNORE" then
            Return "IGNORE"
        End

        If llm_reply.starts_with("SEARCH:") then
            Create query equal to llm_reply.replace("SEARCH:", "").trim()
            Say "[Agent] Searching: " + query
            Create search_result equal to tool_web_search(query)
            messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
            messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "Search result for '" + query + "': " + search_result)

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("WEATHER:") then
            Create loc equal to llm_reply.replace("WEATHER:", "").trim()
            Say "[Agent] Weather: " + loc
            Create w_result equal to tool_weather(loc)
            messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
            messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = w_result)

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("CALCULATE:") then
            Create expr equal to llm_reply.replace("CALCULATE:", "").trim()
            Say "[Agent] Calculating: " + expr
            Create calc_result equal to tool_calculate(expr)
            messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
            messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = calc_result)

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("NEWS:") then
            Create topic equal to llm_reply.replace("NEWS:", "").trim()
            Say "[Agent] News: " + topic
            Create n_result equal to tool_news(topic)
            messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
            messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "News result: " + n_result)

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("REMEMBER:") then
            Create fact equal to llm_reply.replace("REMEMBER:", "").trim()
            Say "[Agent] Remembering: " + fact
            memory_save_fact(db, user_id, fact)
            messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
            messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "Fact saved: " + fact)

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("LEARN:") then
            Create learn_data equal to llm_reply.replace("LEARN:", "").trim()
            Create parts equal to learn_data.split("|")
            If length(parts) == 2 then
                Create topic equal to parts[0].trim()
                Create knowledge equal to parts[1].trim()
                Say "[Agent] Learning: " + topic
                memory_save_knowledge(db, topic, knowledge)
                messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
                messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "Knowledge saved: " + topic)
            End

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("GENERATE_IMAGE:") then
            Create prompt equal to llm_reply.replace("GENERATE_IMAGE:", "").trim()
            Say "[Agent] Generating image: " + prompt
            Create img_url equal to tool_generate_image(prompt)
            messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
            messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "Image URL: " + img_url + " (Include this URL in your next message).")

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("CREATE_ROLE:") then
            If username is not equal to "abneesh.dev" then
                messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "ERROR: Only abneesh.dev can execute admin commands.")
                Continue
            End
            Create role_data equal to llm_reply.replace("CREATE_ROLE:", "").trim()
            Create parts equal to role_data.split("|")
            If length(parts) >= 2 then
                Create role_name equal to parts[0].trim()
                Create color_hex equal to parts[1].trim()
                Create permissions equal to "0"
                If length(parts) == 3 then
                    Set permissions to parts[2].trim()
                End
                Say "[Agent] Creating role: " + role_name
                Create result equal to tool_create_role(guild_id, token, role_name, color_hex, permissions)
                messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
                messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = result)
            End

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("CREATE_CHANNEL:") then
            If username is not equal to "abneesh.dev" then
                messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "ERROR: Only abneesh.dev can execute admin commands.")
                Continue
            End
            Create channel_data equal to llm_reply.replace("CREATE_CHANNEL:", "").trim()
            Create parts equal to channel_data.split("|")
            If length(parts) >= 2 then
                Create channel_name equal to parts[0].trim()
                Create ch_type equal to parts[1].trim()
                Say "[Agent] Creating channel: " + channel_name
                Create result equal to tool_create_channel(guild_id, token, channel_name, ch_type)
                messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
                messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = result)
            End

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("SCAN_SERVER:") then
            Say "[Agent] Scanning server..."
            Create result equal to tool_scan_server(guild_id, token)
            messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
            messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "Server layout: " + result)

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("BROADCAST:") then
            Note: Allow BROADCAST for founder AND autonomous triggers
            If username is not equal to "abneesh.dev" and is_autonomous is not equal to True then
                messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = "ERROR: Only the Founder or autonomous system can broadcast.")
                Continue
            End
            Create b_data equal to llm_reply.replace("BROADCAST:", "").trim()
            Create parts equal to b_data.split("|")
            If length(parts) >= 2 then
                Create target_id equal to parts[0].trim()
                Create msg_text equal to parts[1].trim()
                Say "[Agent] Broadcasting to " + target_id
                Create result equal to tool_broadcast(target_id, token, msg_text)
                messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
                messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = result)
            End

        Otherwise If llm_reply.starts_with("CHECK_GITHUB:") then
            Say "[Agent] Checking GitHub..."
            Create result equal to tool_check_github("trigger")
            messages.add(Map with role = "assistant" and content = llm_reply)
            messages.add(Map with role = "system" and content = result)

        Otherwise
            memory_save_message(db, user_id, username, "user", user_message)
            memory_save_message(db, user_id, username, "assistant", llm_reply)
            Return llm_reply
        End
    End

    Return "I've reached my processing limit for this request. Please try again."
End
